{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/PrivacyManifests","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Traffluent"}],"title":"Privacy Manifests"},"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What each module can collect, the required-reason APIs it calls, and the privacy manifest it ships, so you can fill in your app’s own manifest and privacy labels."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Choosing what to record","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/WhatGoesWhere","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/ChangingEvents","doc:\/\/Traffluent\/documentation\/Traffluent\/IdentifyingPeople"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Choosing-what-to-record"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Traffluent collects nothing on its own. It records only the events your app tracks and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context your app turns on: every kind of automatic instrumentation and every standard enricher is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"opt in. It sends records only to the destinations your app gives a delivery, to endpoints your app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names. None of it is used for tracking as Apple defines it: no module links what it records with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other companies’ data, reads the advertising identifier, fingerprints the device, or works around"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the user’s consent or App Tracking Transparency. Every manifest declares "},{"code":"NSPrivacyTracking","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and lists no tracking domains."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each module that can produce data of one of Apple’s collected data types ships a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy"},{"text":" declaring it. SwiftPM and Bazel both put it in a resource bundle named","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traffluent_<Module>.bundle"},{"text":", which Xcode and rules_apple copy into your app, where Xcode’s privacy","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"report finds it. A module your app doesn’t link adds nothing to the report.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Required-reason-APIs","text":"Required-reason APIs","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No Traffluent module calls an API on Apple’s list of required-reason APIs, so every manifest’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes"},{"text":" is empty. The list’s categories are file timestamps","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp"},{"text":"), system boot time","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime"},{"text":"), disk space","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace"},{"text":"), active keyboards","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryActiveKeyboards"},{"text":") and user defaults","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults"},{"text":"). The modules that come nearest:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Module","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What it calls"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why none is a required-reason API"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence","type":"reference"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"swift-system’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"FileDescriptor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"open","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"read","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"write","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"seek","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"resize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"close","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), ","type":"text"},{"code":"fsync","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"unlink","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"FileManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"createDirectory","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"setAttributes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the file protection class), ","type":"text"},{"code":"contentsOfDirectory","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"isExcludedFromBackup","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It reads no file’s timestamps, size from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stat"},{"type":"text","text":", or the volume’s free space: a segment’s size is the offset "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"seek"},{"type":"text","text":" returns at its end, and the store bounds itself by the bytes it has written."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LifecycleTracking\/documentation\/LifecycleTracking"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileManager.fileExists"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type"